class TamTamProperties(ModeDecays, CymbalProperties):
    """A TAM-TAM: the GS gongs (ASIA set 53's Asian, Big and Small Gong; the
    ETHNIC set's). MEASURED (examples/gong_fit.py) on Iowa MIS's 22", 28" and
    40" tam-tams, one strike a take left to ring (30-117 s), pp/mf/ff:

      * THE MODES, from the ff take's first second: a share per octave to 8
        kHz (the strongest 200 overall all sat under 1.7 kHz, where a tam-
        tam's modes are densest), as ratios to the lowest within 30 dB of the
        strongest -- 136, 84 and 66 Hz -- and each mode's level 30-130 ms
        after the strike (mode_gains, read at ff: mode_stroke_ref_db 0).
      * EACH MODE'S OWN DECAY (ModeDecays; tonelib's D, half the dB/s): the
        lowest ring at 1-3 dB/s, a minute to fall away; the top 8-20.
      * THE STRIKE'S DYNAMICS ARE THE PLATE'S NONLINEARITY. A soft strike is
        the low modes alone: in every pp take nothing above 250 Hz clears the
        recording's noise. From mf to ff the 4 kHz band gains 10-20 dB on the
        lowest mode -- mode_stroke_tilt, dB per octave per dB of stroke, from
        mf against ff (the pp takes' noise flattened it).
      * THE BLOOM: at ff the 1-4 kHz bands go on rising after the strike and
        peak at 0.45-1.25 s, 10-20 dB over where they began -- the cascade
        that IS the tam-tam's swell, where a crash's is 0.1-0.4 s. The crash's
        banded, scattered late copy (bloom_banded), slower, its gain growing
        with the strike (bloom_gain_slope) so a soft one does not swell.
        Searched (gong_fit.py --fit-bloom, mf and ff of all three): 0.3 s,
        gain 3, at 2.5 kHz -- its swell (bloom_swell 1) peaking near 0.6 s.
        A flat optimum (5.3-6.3 dB over the 24 tried): the grid holds the
        bloom loosely, the ear will say more.
    Band-by-time error over the nine takes 44 -> 7.4 dB; mf and ff 4.5-7.6.
    pp stays 13-15: a soft strike is the lowest mode ALONE, steeper than the
    mf-ff tilt carried down -- a gong roll lives in mf-ff (Tokei's 44-127)."""
    one_shot = True
    release_floor_db = -50.0
    # ONE PLATE: a strike on a ringing gong adds to its ring, and the two are
    # the same modes -- folded into one strike's rows (blockrender fold_restrike)
    fold_restrike = True
    attack_time = 0.004            # a felt mallet, not a stick
    chiff_volume = 0.2             # ...so little strike noise
    sustain_jitter = 0.02
    decay_db = 0.0
    decay_register_slope = 0.0     # one gong, one size: no register law
    aftersound_fraction = 0.0      # each mode's own decay, measured
    mode_stroke_ref_db = 0.0
    bloom_banded = True
    bloom_seconds = 0.3
    bloom_center_hz = 2500.0
    bloom_octaves = 1.5
    bloom_gain = 3.0
    bloom_gain_slope = 1.5
    bloom_scatter = 1.0
    bloom_swell = 1.0


